1
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:43,910
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,320 --> 00:01:46,880
[Episode 14]

3
00:01:52,229 --> 00:01:53,039
Excuse me.

4
00:01:53,039 --> 00:01:53,840
May I ask how much

5
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:55,500
longer till we reach Nanjing?

6
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:56,430
Let me check.

7
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:58,479
We'll reach Bengbu
in a bit more than 3 hours.

8
00:01:58,479 --> 00:01:59,920
The stop following it is Nanjing.

9
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:00,280
Thank you.

10
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:01,740
Alright. Just be patient.

11
00:02:04,150 --> 00:02:05,840
Keep your voice down.

12
00:02:07,310 --> 00:02:08,030
First, throw a two.

13
00:02:08,030 --> 00:02:09,240
T-Then eight, nine, ten, jack, queen.

14
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:10,570
It'll be a win, won't it?

15
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:12,840
Isn't it a sure win
when these cards are out?

16
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:14,240
Do you even know how to play?

17
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:15,640
What the heck is all this?

18
00:02:16,230 --> 00:02:17,240
Look at these cards.

19
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:19,040
Winning cards they are, I'd say.

20
00:02:19,430 --> 00:02:20,690
Do you know how to play?

21
00:02:21,310 --> 00:02:21,910
With a joker

22
00:02:21,910 --> 00:02:22,960
and a straight, I'll win.

23
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:23,680
You know?

24
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:25,940
Go away if you don't know how poker works.

25
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:38,470
Emergency notice!

26
00:02:39,079 --> 00:02:41,120
If there are any medical workers on board,

27
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:42,720
please hurry to carriage 14.

28
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:45,400
If there are any medical workers on board,

29
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:47,000
please hurry to carriage 14.

30
00:02:49,310 --> 00:02:49,910
No one's coming to help.

31
00:02:49,910 --> 00:02:50,680
Repeat the announcement.

32
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:51,810
Quick, say it again!

33
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:52,560
Is there a doctor?

34
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:53,710
We're trying to get one.

35
00:02:53,710 --> 00:02:54,310
-We're trying.
-Let me through.

36
00:02:54,310 --> 00:02:54,800
There will be a doctor soon.

37
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:56,060
Please let me through.

38
00:02:57,470 --> 00:02:58,520
W-Who are you?

39
00:02:58,520 --> 00:02:59,630
He's a doctor!

40
00:02:59,710 --> 00:03:00,430
You're a doctor, huh?

41
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:01,150
Doctor!

42
00:03:01,150 --> 00:03:01,750
Check on her.

43
00:03:01,750 --> 00:03:02,520
What doesn't feel right?

44
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:04,680
My stomach hurts, and I'm dizzy.

45
00:03:05,150 --> 00:03:05,630
Dizzy.

46
00:03:05,630 --> 00:03:07,400
Any history of high blood pressure?

47
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:08,190
No.

48
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:09,310
How far along are you?

49
00:03:09,310 --> 00:03:10,370
Over eight months.

50
00:03:10,590 --> 00:03:11,750
Thirty-two weeks and five days!

51
00:03:11,750 --> 00:03:12,280
That's right.

52
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:13,120
Now let her lie flat.

53
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:14,080
Nice and slow.

54
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:16,280
-Slowly. Watch your head.
-Here you go.

55
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:17,470
When the pain first kicked in,

56
00:03:17,470 --> 00:03:18,750
I thought I could bear it for a while.

57
00:03:18,750 --> 00:03:19,610
Bend your legs.

58
00:03:19,630 --> 00:03:20,590
-Get a curtain here. Quick!
-But it got worse and worse.

59
00:03:20,590 --> 00:03:21,840
Hurry, get a curtain here!

60
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:22,240
Make it quick!

61
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:23,100
You'll be fine.

62
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:26,960
How long is the interval

63
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:27,870
between pain attacks?

64
00:03:27,870 --> 00:03:29,360
The pain comes about

65
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:30,590
every five minutes.

66
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:32,110
What's there to do, doctor?

67
00:03:32,110 --> 00:03:33,310
Will my baby be okay?

68
00:03:33,310 --> 00:03:34,280
It'll be okay.

69
00:03:34,430 --> 00:03:35,190
Train attendant,

70
00:03:35,190 --> 00:03:36,240
notify the next station

71
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:37,840
to arrange for an ambulance.

72
00:03:37,870 --> 00:03:39,079
I've notified them.

73
00:03:39,310 --> 00:03:40,430
Ask the receiving hospital

74
00:03:40,430 --> 00:03:41,079
to get prepared

75
00:03:41,079 --> 00:03:42,190
to rescue a newborn.

76
00:03:42,190 --> 00:03:43,310
Breech presentation.

77
00:03:43,310 --> 00:03:44,440
What does that mean?

78
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:45,870
Never mind. Just say it to them!

79
00:03:45,870 --> 00:03:46,630
Okay, got it.

80
00:03:46,870 --> 00:03:47,910
Quickly notify the doctors

81
00:03:47,910 --> 00:03:48,840
in the hospital.

82
00:03:49,310 --> 00:03:50,079
Lie on your side.

83
00:03:50,079 --> 00:03:51,210
Here, nice and slow.

84
00:03:51,310 --> 00:03:51,840
Make it quick!

85
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:52,630
Doctor,

86
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:54,310
am I going to die?

87
00:03:54,310 --> 00:03:55,030
No.

88
00:03:55,710 --> 00:03:58,240
Will my baby be okay?

89
00:03:58,280 --> 00:03:59,470
Now, look in my eyes.

90
00:03:59,710 --> 00:04:00,680
Stay composed.

91
00:04:01,190 --> 00:04:02,030
I promise that both

92
00:04:02,030 --> 00:04:03,590
you and your baby will be fine,

93
00:04:03,590 --> 00:04:04,400
alright?

94
00:04:04,590 --> 00:04:06,430
Next, just do as I say.

95
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:08,590
Breathe in through your nose
and out through your mouth.

96
00:04:08,590 --> 00:04:09,360
Can you do that?

97
00:04:09,360 --> 00:04:10,680
Come on, breathe in.

98
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:15,080
Breathe out.

99
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:17,600
Right.

100
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:18,190
Again.

101
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:19,360
Breathe in.

102
00:04:21,720 --> 00:04:22,560
Breathe out.

103
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:26,600
That's right. You're doing great.

104
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:28,430
Adjust your breathing.
Repeat what you just did.

105
00:04:28,430 --> 00:04:29,240
Breathe in.

106
00:04:47,159 --> 00:04:48,090
I won't drink it.

107
00:04:57,190 --> 00:04:58,520
I heard from Zhengguang

108
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:00,700
that Liu Zhengliang left.

109
00:05:02,750 --> 00:05:03,600
Are you upset?

110
00:05:04,310 --> 00:05:05,240
Not really.

111
00:05:06,390 --> 00:05:07,990
There's nothing between us.

112
00:05:09,270 --> 00:05:11,200
Then what was on your mind just now?

113
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:13,560
N-Nothing.

114
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:14,690
I simply spaced out.

115
00:05:17,190 --> 00:05:18,650
The principle I stick to is

116
00:05:20,070 --> 00:05:22,830
that you should fight for what you like

117
00:05:22,950 --> 00:05:24,750
and spare no effort while you're at it.

118
00:05:24,750 --> 00:05:25,560
Try your best

119
00:05:26,430 --> 00:05:27,750
and leave no regrets.

120
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:31,340
If you can't stand him being away,

121
00:05:31,750 --> 00:05:33,360
I'll go to the South with you

122
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:35,040
to bring him back.

123
00:05:35,270 --> 00:05:36,120
Forget it.

124
00:05:37,070 --> 00:05:38,680
He's in a special situation.

125
00:05:38,680 --> 00:05:40,310
Why do we have to force him?

126
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:46,600
Then haven't you thought about

127
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:48,330
building a career in the South?

128
00:05:50,870 --> 00:05:52,390
What can I do there?

129
00:05:52,630 --> 00:05:53,870
The funeral business

130
00:05:53,870 --> 00:05:55,159
varies with regions.

131
00:05:55,430 --> 00:05:56,870
There's a fixed group of practitioners

132
00:05:56,870 --> 00:05:58,159
in every area.

133
00:05:58,390 --> 00:05:59,750
How do I even get started?

134
00:05:59,750 --> 00:06:01,480
If I leave this line of business

135
00:06:01,750 --> 00:06:02,870
and lose my job,

136
00:06:02,950 --> 00:06:04,000
how do I live on?

137
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:06,430
How do I support myself?

138
00:06:06,430 --> 00:06:07,560
By relying on Liu Zhengliang?

139
00:06:07,560 --> 00:06:08,430
No way.

140
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:11,190
Let me be clear with you.

141
00:06:11,190 --> 00:06:12,000
Ai Chen

142
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:14,240
can be someone's wife,

143
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:15,510
but she can't just be

144
00:06:15,510 --> 00:06:16,750
someone's wife.

145
00:06:16,950 --> 00:06:17,750
You get it?

146
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:19,360
Hearing you say that,

147
00:06:20,390 --> 00:06:21,630
I feel so relieved.

148
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:29,360
So that was a test?

149
00:06:29,510 --> 00:06:31,240
I was afraid you'd act foolish.

150
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,800
Give me some credit, will you?

151
00:06:40,560 --> 00:06:43,240
Liu Zhengliang doesn't have
a great personality.

152
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:44,560
What do you see in him?

153
00:06:45,430 --> 00:06:46,830
Is it that he's scholarly

154
00:06:47,270 --> 00:06:47,870
and smart?

155
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:54,600
At first,

156
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:57,120
I did like him for being a doctor.

157
00:06:57,510 --> 00:06:58,800
But later,

158
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:02,240
I realized that I also liked

159
00:07:03,740 --> 00:07:05,470
the vulnerability he carries.

160
00:07:06,630 --> 00:07:07,430
What?

161
00:07:08,750 --> 00:07:10,310
I mean it's like he'd break

162
00:07:10,310 --> 00:07:11,800
at the slightest touch.

163
00:07:14,510 --> 00:07:15,440
Anything wrong?

164
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:17,920
Girls usually like tough men.

165
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:20,160
Who would fall for a vulnerable guy?

166
00:07:21,390 --> 00:07:22,190
Sweetie,

167
00:07:22,630 --> 00:07:24,760
you think you're picking crisps here?

168
00:07:53,870 --> 00:07:54,800
Liu Zhengliang,

169
00:07:54,870 --> 00:07:56,830
you really left at the right time.

170
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:06,980
[Bengbu Station]

171
00:08:17,070 --> 00:08:18,310
Here comes the doctor.

172
00:08:18,310 --> 00:08:19,310
Hurry.

173
00:08:19,310 --> 00:08:20,070
Thank you.

174
00:08:20,070 --> 00:08:20,390
No problem.

175
00:08:20,390 --> 00:08:21,920
Put her on nasal oxygen now.

176
00:08:23,040 --> 00:08:24,160
What's the situation?

177
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:25,000
Aged 31.

178
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,000
At 32 weeks and 5 days of gestation.

179
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:27,240
Contractions every three minutes,

180
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:27,950
lasting 60 seconds

181
00:08:27,950 --> 00:08:29,360
at high intensity levels.

182
00:08:29,360 --> 00:08:30,430
Any pelvic exam done yet?

183
00:08:30,430 --> 00:08:31,190
No, for conditions

184
00:08:31,190 --> 00:08:32,120
didn't allow it.

185
00:08:32,600 --> 00:08:33,659
Does it still hurt?

186
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:34,360
I'm much better now.

187
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:35,559
The pain has eased up.

188
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:37,510
If it doesn't hurt much,

189
00:08:37,510 --> 00:08:38,270
just hold on a bit

190
00:08:38,270 --> 00:08:39,000
and get off the train now.

191
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,120
The ambulance is right outside.

192
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:41,390
Alright. You're perfectly fine.

193
00:08:41,390 --> 00:08:41,720
This way.

194
00:08:41,720 --> 00:08:42,360
Careful.

195
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:42,840
Slowly.

196
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:44,300
Don't forget the clothes.

197
00:08:44,510 --> 00:08:45,120
Nice and slow.

198
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:46,150
Passengers nearby, please make way.

199
00:08:46,150 --> 00:08:46,880
Hold on to me.

200
00:08:47,390 --> 00:08:49,390
Passengers ahead, please make way.

201
00:08:49,390 --> 00:08:50,440
Boarding passengers,

202
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:51,440
please step back.

203
00:08:52,510 --> 00:08:52,790
Careful.

204
00:08:52,790 --> 00:08:54,360
There's a pregnant woman here.

205
00:08:54,360 --> 00:08:55,320
Watch your step.

206
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:56,480
Watch your step.

207
00:08:57,320 --> 00:08:58,120
Nice and slow.

208
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:03,080
One, two, three!

209
00:09:04,240 --> 00:09:05,170
Slowly lie down.

210
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:06,120
Slowly.

211
00:09:08,360 --> 00:09:09,150
Careful.

212
00:09:09,240 --> 00:09:10,840
I think my water just broke.

213
00:09:12,790 --> 00:09:13,510
Doctor!

214
00:09:13,510 --> 00:09:14,440
Cover her with clothes.

215
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:15,120
Doctor!

216
00:09:15,120 --> 00:09:15,550
It's okay.

217
00:09:15,550 --> 00:09:16,550
Just lie down.

218
00:09:16,550 --> 00:09:17,680
-Careful.
-Doctor!

219
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:19,810
Give me sterile gloves.

220
00:09:19,870 --> 00:09:21,670
It's okay, honey. Hang in there!

221
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:23,280
It's going to be fine.

222
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:24,820
It hurts so bad.

223
00:09:25,360 --> 00:09:26,240
I can't take it anymore.

224
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:26,960
This is bad.

225
00:09:27,150 --> 00:09:27,960
The umbilical cord prolapsed.

226
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:29,360
The baby is still inside.

227
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:30,600
We have 5 minutes at most.

228
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:31,440
The baby's in danger.

229
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:32,510
The cord has to be pushed back in.

230
00:09:32,510 --> 00:09:33,670
Go! Get her into the ambulance now!

231
00:09:33,670 --> 00:09:34,360
Move!

232
00:09:34,870 --> 00:09:35,630
Doctor!

233
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:37,480
What about your luggage?

234
00:09:44,070 --> 00:09:46,370
[Bengbu City Emergency Rescue Center]

235
00:09:46,420 --> 00:09:48,150
[120]

236
00:09:48,790 --> 00:09:50,320
Blood pressure 140 over 95.

237
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:51,840
Blood oxygen 95%.

238
00:09:54,120 --> 00:09:55,960
Any delivery kit or episiotomy kit?

239
00:09:55,960 --> 00:09:56,600
Yes.

240
00:09:56,670 --> 00:09:57,530
Pass them to me.

241
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:00,160
You have to push hard.

242
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:02,600
Come on. Push.

243
00:10:02,600 --> 00:10:03,510
Adjust your breathing.

244
00:10:03,510 --> 00:10:04,390
Breathe, honey.

245
00:10:04,390 --> 00:10:05,000
Breathe.

246
00:10:05,030 --> 00:10:05,670
Push!

247
00:10:05,670 --> 00:10:07,000
Yes. Bite me if you have to, honey.

248
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:07,840
Bite me hard.

249
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:08,550
Come on.

250
00:10:08,750 --> 00:10:09,910
Push hard!

251
00:10:11,950 --> 00:10:13,550
[Bengbu City Emergency Rescue Center]

252
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:13,200
Honey, hang in there.

253
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:13,630
Honey.

254
00:10:13,630 --> 00:10:14,670
Push harder. Push!

255
00:10:14,670 --> 00:10:15,550
Come on, push!

256
00:10:16,870 --> 00:10:17,930
It'll be over soon.

257
00:10:19,910 --> 00:10:20,720
Push!

258
00:10:20,750 --> 00:10:21,550
Harder!

259
00:10:21,600 --> 00:10:22,360
The baby's born.

260
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:23,320
The baby's born.

261
00:10:23,320 --> 00:10:24,650
Honey, the baby's born!

262
00:10:25,510 --> 00:10:27,170
Curved forceps and scissors.

263
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:36,150
[Bengbu City Emergency Rescue Center]

264
00:10:55,390 --> 00:10:56,590
Come on, sweetheart.

265
00:10:56,960 --> 00:10:57,960
Let me carry you.

266
00:10:58,150 --> 00:10:59,910
My precious little girl.

267
00:11:01,390 --> 00:11:02,590
It's okay. It's okay.

268
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:04,080
Alright.

269
00:11:04,320 --> 00:11:04,960
Your feet.

270
00:11:05,080 --> 00:11:07,210
We're finally getting home after such

271
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:08,550
a long stay in the hospital.

272
00:11:08,550 --> 00:11:09,150
How am I

273
00:11:09,150 --> 00:11:10,360
feeling a bit uneasy?

274
00:11:10,360 --> 00:11:12,030
It's great news
that our daughter's being discharged.

275
00:11:12,030 --> 00:11:12,790
Don't overthink it.

276
00:11:12,790 --> 00:11:13,870
Come on, let's go.

277
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,120
Y-You push the wheelchair.

278
00:11:15,120 --> 00:11:15,510
I'll take this.

279
00:11:15,510 --> 00:11:17,270
Sweetheart, we're going home!

280
00:11:15,970 --> 00:11:19,500
[Yellow Zone]

281
00:11:17,480 --> 00:11:18,000
Let's go.

282
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:18,630
There we go.

283
00:11:18,630 --> 00:11:19,440
I can manage.

284
00:11:19,500 --> 00:11:22,110
[Keep the ward clean and tidy]

285
00:11:40,290 --> 00:11:43,660
♪ The melting snow and the warm wind ♪

286
00:11:43,850 --> 00:11:46,150
♪ The flowers bloom again ♪

287
00:11:47,270 --> 00:11:49,000
Today is such a wonderful day.

288
00:11:47,460 --> 00:11:53,160
♪ It's spring; it's a remedy ♪

289
00:11:50,240 --> 00:11:51,630
Everyone in our hospital

290
00:11:51,630 --> 00:11:52,720
is happy for you.

291
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:55,480
Inside these two big bags

292
00:11:55,070 --> 00:11:58,680
♪ Stop and go, travelling separately ♪

293
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:57,550
is the medication
Zhang Jiao needs to take routinely

294
00:11:57,550 --> 00:11:58,550
for her recovery.

295
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:01,200
It's also a token of goodwill

296
00:11:58,940 --> 00:12:01,020
♪ At the next intersection ♪

297
00:12:01,440 --> 00:12:02,550
from all the hospital staff.

298
00:12:02,550 --> 00:12:04,300
♪ You and I ♪

299
00:12:02,910 --> 00:12:04,670
We wish the child all the best,

300
00:12:04,960 --> 00:12:06,100
and may all things go well.

301
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:08,780
♪ Travel light ♪

302
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:08,390
Thanks. Thank you, President.

303
00:12:08,390 --> 00:12:09,030
Thank you.

304
00:12:09,030 --> 00:12:09,750
Thank you.

305
00:12:10,060 --> 00:12:16,190
♪ Put the past weighing on my back
into the moon ♪

306
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:11,790
Jiao,

307
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:14,840
we hope you grow up healthy and happy.

308
00:12:17,530 --> 00:12:22,690
♪ Longing makes me wake up ♪

309
00:12:19,720 --> 00:12:21,200
T-Thank you.

310
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:27,290
♪ To the open window♪

311
00:12:28,170 --> 00:12:34,880
♪ Softly, the person in my dream
is like the moonlight ♪

312
00:12:35,400 --> 00:12:39,570
♪ Falling on my heart softly
and taking me ♪

313
00:12:38,430 --> 00:12:43,040
[Emergency]

314
00:12:39,780 --> 00:12:42,400
♪ To our old familiar place ♪

315
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:41,790
Thank you.

316
00:12:43,040 --> 00:12:49,450
♪ Slowly, the petals falls to the center
of the lake when I miss you ♪

317
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:45,300
Jiao, you're finally going home.

318
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:46,460
Time to go home.

319
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:47,900
Thank you, Dr. Che.

320
00:12:49,720 --> 00:12:50,910
Many thanks to Xiaoximen Hospital!

321
00:12:50,310 --> 00:12:54,380
♪ Ripples echo through the years,
with our shadows faced each other ♪

322
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:53,870
Let's go home!

323
00:12:54,760 --> 00:13:00,230
♪ We were together on the way we came ♪

324
00:12:55,600 --> 00:12:56,730
Have a safe journey.

325
00:12:58,720 --> 00:13:02,510
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

326
00:13:02,630 --> 00:13:09,120
[Emergency Access Route; No Parking]

327
00:13:13,910 --> 00:13:15,240
Mingming!

328
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:17,120
Who are you?

329
00:13:20,270 --> 00:13:21,390
Put me down!

330
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:22,360
Down!

331
00:13:24,870 --> 00:13:25,670
Huang.

332
00:13:26,630 --> 00:13:27,760
You're back, buddy.

333
00:13:27,790 --> 00:13:28,670
Yes, I'm back.

334
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,130
T-This is Zhang Hao.

335
00:13:32,430 --> 00:13:33,390
Nice to meet you.

336
00:13:33,790 --> 00:13:34,920
Nice to meet you too.

337
00:14:11,390 --> 00:14:12,720
Fortunately, it was handled in time.

338
00:14:11,610 --> 00:14:13,470
[Welcome baby]

339
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:13,790
So your wife is fine.

340
00:14:13,790 --> 00:14:15,240
Let her stay a while in hospital
for observation.

341
00:14:14,310 --> 00:14:15,900
[How to welcome a newborn]

342
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:16,750
Thank you for your help, doctor.

343
00:14:16,750 --> 00:14:17,750
Thank you so much.

344
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:26,510
[Fetal sex identification
for non-medical reasons is prohibited]

345
00:14:25,910 --> 00:14:26,720
Excuse me.

346
00:14:26,530 --> 00:14:29,700
[Fetal sex identification
for non-medical reasons is prohibited]

347
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:28,630
Hello.

348
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:30,000
I...

349
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,460
Thank you so much, doctor.

350
00:14:31,870 --> 00:14:32,510
My wife and child

351
00:14:32,510 --> 00:14:33,480
wouldn't have made it without you.

352
00:14:33,480 --> 00:14:34,080
Thank you, doctor.

353
00:14:34,080 --> 00:14:34,550
Thank you so much.

354
00:14:34,550 --> 00:14:35,270
You're welcome.

355
00:14:35,270 --> 00:14:36,000
Well,

356
00:14:36,030 --> 00:14:37,360
no more thanks for now.

357
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:38,240
There's a more

358
00:14:38,240 --> 00:14:40,150
prominent problem to solve at the moment.

359
00:14:40,150 --> 00:14:40,960
Well,

360
00:14:40,960 --> 00:14:42,750
I should have arrived

361
00:14:42,750 --> 00:14:44,000
in Nanjing by now.

362
00:14:44,030 --> 00:14:44,790
But we had to get off

363
00:14:44,790 --> 00:14:45,990
in Bengbu, didn't we?

364
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:47,240
So... about

365
00:14:48,080 --> 00:14:49,080
the train ticket,

366
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:50,390
do you think you can...

367
00:14:50,960 --> 00:14:51,630
No problem.

368
00:14:51,630 --> 00:14:52,030
I'll buy you

369
00:14:52,030 --> 00:14:54,160
the best seat on the high-speed train.

370
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:56,120
Here's the thing.

371
00:14:56,630 --> 00:14:57,840
Actually, I was heading

372
00:14:57,840 --> 00:14:58,840
for Nanjing just to transfer

373
00:14:58,840 --> 00:14:59,720
to Fuzhou.

374
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:01,150
But now it seems

375
00:15:01,150 --> 00:15:02,840
I'll miss that train too.

376
00:15:08,670 --> 00:15:09,840
Here's all the cash I have on me.

377
00:15:09,840 --> 00:15:10,840
Look. Take it all.

378
00:15:10,840 --> 00:15:11,630
See if it's enough.

379
00:15:11,630 --> 00:15:11,960
If not,

380
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:12,720
I'll go get some more

381
00:15:12,720 --> 00:15:13,200
from the ATM now.

382
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:14,030
Just give me a sec, doctor.

383
00:15:14,030 --> 00:15:14,870
No, don't.

384
00:15:15,320 --> 00:15:16,600
It's more than enough.

385
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:18,240
How about this?

386
00:15:18,240 --> 00:15:19,080
Leave me

387
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:20,120
your contact info.

388
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:20,840
So I can return the extra

389
00:15:20,840 --> 00:15:22,440
to you after I refund or change

390
00:15:22,440 --> 00:15:23,750
the ticket at the train station.

391
00:15:23,750 --> 00:15:24,440
No need, doctor.

392
00:15:24,440 --> 00:15:25,030
Consider

393
00:15:25,030 --> 00:15:26,910
the extra as a token of my appreciation.

394
00:15:26,910 --> 00:15:28,120
Just take all the money.

395
00:15:28,120 --> 00:15:30,380
Buy yourself clothes or something else.

396
00:15:33,870 --> 00:15:34,550
Fine then.

397
00:15:35,030 --> 00:15:35,840
Well,

398
00:15:36,550 --> 00:15:37,610
congratulations.

399
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:38,790
Goodbye.

400
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:39,630
Thank you.

401
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:41,500
Take care, doctor.

402
00:15:42,240 --> 00:15:44,540
[Bengbu Chaokang Hospital]

403
00:15:49,150 --> 00:15:52,940
[Bengbu Chaokang Hospital]

404
00:15:55,790 --> 00:15:57,200
Sir, to the train station.

405
00:15:57,200 --> 00:15:58,670
I'm in a rush. Thanks.

406
00:16:05,480 --> 00:16:06,200
Bro,

407
00:16:06,510 --> 00:16:07,710
what happened to you?

408
00:16:09,080 --> 00:16:10,010
What do you mean?

409
00:16:10,320 --> 00:16:11,840
There's so much blood on you.

410
00:16:11,840 --> 00:16:14,240
How am I supposed to take
other passengers?

411
00:16:14,670 --> 00:16:16,470
None of it has gotten on your car.

412
00:16:17,630 --> 00:16:19,120
But it smells.

413
00:16:19,200 --> 00:16:20,320
What smell?

414
00:16:20,320 --> 00:16:21,200
I've been in here for so long.

415
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:21,840
Just drive.

416
00:16:21,840 --> 00:16:22,840
Time is pressing.

417
00:16:25,240 --> 00:16:26,720
Are you from the Northeast,
given that accent?

418
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:27,720
No, maybe you are.

419
00:16:27,790 --> 00:16:29,520
Yes, I am, through and through.

420
00:16:30,750 --> 00:16:32,470
How come there are
Northeasterners everywhere?

421
00:16:32,470 --> 00:16:33,070
Excuse me?

422
00:16:33,270 --> 00:16:34,600
What's wrong with the Northeasterners?

423
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:35,460
Nothing wrong.

424
00:16:40,390 --> 00:16:42,080
Listen, get out of my car.

425
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:42,790
I'm not doing

426
00:16:42,790 --> 00:16:43,850
business with you.

427
00:16:44,870 --> 00:16:46,080
What do you mean, sir?

428
00:16:46,150 --> 00:16:46,870
Why can't you finish the ride?

429
00:16:46,870 --> 00:16:47,840
I'm in a hurry.

430
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:48,910
I'm telling you,

431
00:16:48,910 --> 00:16:50,080
I hate you regional bigots

432
00:16:50,080 --> 00:16:51,210
more than anything.

433
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:52,440
File a complaint if you want.

434
00:16:52,440 --> 00:16:53,120
I don't care.

435
00:16:53,120 --> 00:16:54,920
Who's a regional bigot now? I...

436
00:16:56,150 --> 00:16:58,080
I was also born in the Northeast, sir.

437
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:59,440
Once I refuse to serve, you're

438
00:16:59,440 --> 00:17:00,910
suddenly a Northeasterner?

439
00:17:00,910 --> 00:17:01,960
Trying to buddy up with me, huh?

440
00:17:01,960 --> 00:17:04,310
-Get out of my car now.
-I really don't have time for this fuss.

441
00:17:04,310 --> 00:17:05,069
I'm in a real hurry.

442
00:17:05,069 --> 00:17:06,270
I'm going to miss my train.

443
00:17:06,270 --> 00:17:07,400
Can you just drive?

444
00:17:07,680 --> 00:17:08,550
You think I'd care?

445
00:17:08,550 --> 00:17:09,680
Get out of my car now.

446
00:17:09,880 --> 00:17:11,010
I'm ending the ride.

447
00:17:14,069 --> 00:17:15,000
Get a move on!

448
00:17:31,350 --> 00:17:32,680
Is that her ex-husband?

449
00:17:44,510 --> 00:17:46,240
Did you go traveling or were you

450
00:17:46,480 --> 00:17:47,720
fleeing from a famine?

451
00:17:47,720 --> 00:17:49,440
I went traveling, of course.

452
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:52,840
But it was worse than
fleeing a famine at first.

453
00:17:53,720 --> 00:17:55,200
I made a trip to Jiagedaqi

454
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:58,200
and got lost
in the Greater Khingan Mountains.

455
00:17:58,200 --> 00:17:59,000
Wait. So...

456
00:17:59,310 --> 00:18:00,830
you got lost while traveling?

457
00:18:00,830 --> 00:18:01,920
Really?

458
00:18:02,070 --> 00:18:03,870
Why would I lie to you about that?

459
00:18:04,960 --> 00:18:07,090
I brought you some local specialties.

460
00:18:07,750 --> 00:18:08,830
Hey, Huang,

461
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:10,080
deer antlers for you.

462
00:18:10,680 --> 00:18:11,480
You...

463
00:18:11,720 --> 00:18:12,310
Well...

464
00:18:12,310 --> 00:18:12,880
You...

465
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:14,350
These are very nutritional.

466
00:18:14,350 --> 00:18:16,400
Why squander your money on these?

467
00:18:16,680 --> 00:18:17,750
I have plenty of money.

468
00:18:17,750 --> 00:18:20,160
These can lower blood pressure.
Good stuff.

469
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:21,360
Where is Zhengliang?

470
00:18:21,510 --> 00:18:23,110
He has gone back to the South.

471
00:18:23,790 --> 00:18:24,550
So he eventually went back.

472
00:18:24,550 --> 00:18:25,550
Yes, he did.

473
00:18:26,310 --> 00:18:27,480
Then I'll give this to you.

474
00:18:27,480 --> 00:18:28,680
It's also great stuff.

475
00:18:28,680 --> 00:18:30,140
From the wilderness, too.

476
00:18:31,070 --> 00:18:31,310
Thanks.

477
00:18:31,310 --> 00:18:33,680
I thought I was definitely going to die
back then.

478
00:18:33,680 --> 00:18:35,750
Later on, an Ewenki named Xiwen

479
00:18:35,750 --> 00:18:37,030
saved my life.

480
00:18:37,270 --> 00:18:38,720
I spent half a month there.

481
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:39,960
It felt amazing.

482
00:18:43,310 --> 00:18:44,550
Cheers, Meng.

483
00:18:51,240 --> 00:18:53,920
-Loosen your grip.
-Then prop it up, right?

484
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:54,720
Yes, release.

485
00:18:55,240 --> 00:18:55,790
Right.

486
00:18:56,400 --> 00:18:56,920
Correct.

487
00:18:56,920 --> 00:18:58,640
I got the hang of it.

488
00:19:06,070 --> 00:19:07,130
For the first time,

489
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:09,920
I realized that I had such close bonds

490
00:19:09,960 --> 00:19:11,160
with nature, the forest,

491
00:19:11,160 --> 00:19:12,750
and all kinds of animals.

492
00:19:13,110 --> 00:19:15,000
I even learned how to raise reindeer.

493
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:16,270
Why? Did they fight you for food?

494
00:19:16,270 --> 00:19:17,730
Why else are you so hungry?

495
00:19:20,720 --> 00:19:23,250
Because I couldn't eat anything
on the train.

496
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:25,200
I got used to the food in the mountains,

497
00:19:25,200 --> 00:19:28,460
and couldn't bring myself
to eat instant noodles anymore.

498
00:19:31,440 --> 00:19:32,310
I came back

499
00:19:33,590 --> 00:19:35,270
to deal with two major issues.

500
00:19:35,550 --> 00:19:36,440
First,

501
00:19:36,680 --> 00:19:37,810
I'm going to resign.

502
00:19:38,030 --> 00:19:39,510
The town at the foot of the mountain
where Xiwen lives

503
00:19:39,510 --> 00:19:40,550
is short of doctors.

504
00:19:40,550 --> 00:19:42,110
I plan to settle down there.

505
00:19:42,110 --> 00:19:42,830
What?

506
00:19:43,200 --> 00:19:45,930
You're moving
to the Greater Khingan Mountains?

507
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:49,030
In the past, I only cared about
making money,

508
00:19:49,030 --> 00:19:50,720
which invisibly added

509
00:19:51,070 --> 00:19:53,200
much meaningless pressure on myself.

510
00:19:54,030 --> 00:19:55,680
I even saw you and your father

511
00:19:55,920 --> 00:19:57,650
as burdens that slowed me down.

512
00:19:58,640 --> 00:20:00,440
But now I understand, Mingming.

513
00:20:00,640 --> 00:20:02,310
Huang, I understand now.

514
00:20:02,310 --> 00:20:03,440
Oh, you understand.

515
00:20:04,270 --> 00:20:05,070
Mingming,

516
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:07,270
I apologize to you

517
00:20:07,270 --> 00:20:07,960
for what I said

518
00:20:07,960 --> 00:20:08,920
and did before.

519
00:20:10,440 --> 00:20:11,440
I'm sorry.

520
00:20:13,350 --> 00:20:14,640
No need to apologize.

521
00:20:14,750 --> 00:20:15,880
It's all in the past.

522
00:20:16,160 --> 00:20:17,200
We're already divorced.

523
00:20:17,200 --> 00:20:18,270
We don't owe each other anything.

524
00:20:18,270 --> 00:20:19,130
Oh, about that!

525
00:20:22,160 --> 00:20:24,200
The second major issue I came back for...

526
00:20:24,200 --> 00:20:25,000
What is it?

527
00:20:26,920 --> 00:20:28,200
Let me finish. Let me.

528
00:20:29,310 --> 00:20:30,910
That is, I'm remarrying you.

529
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:34,600
Let's go there together.

530
00:20:35,030 --> 00:20:36,230
What did you just say?

531
00:20:37,200 --> 00:20:38,200
You can't have

532
00:20:38,200 --> 00:20:39,590
a real life anywhere else.

533
00:20:39,590 --> 00:20:40,920
Go and see for yourself.

534
00:20:41,270 --> 00:20:42,530
It's wonderful there.

535
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:44,480
Really.

536
00:20:45,960 --> 00:20:47,960
L-Let go of my hands now.

537
00:20:48,400 --> 00:20:49,880
F-Finish your food first.

538
00:20:50,680 --> 00:20:52,110
-We'll talk later.
-Okay.

539
00:20:52,110 --> 00:20:54,310
Let's tell your father when we get home.

540
00:21:00,110 --> 00:21:01,910
You can't imagine how beautiful

541
00:21:02,350 --> 00:21:03,680
that large body of water

542
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:05,730
and those reindeer are.

543
00:21:06,110 --> 00:21:08,270
That's the life everyone yearns for!

544
00:21:10,070 --> 00:21:11,790
Please hold on tight and stand firm.

545
00:21:11,790 --> 00:21:14,400
Hold the handrail tightly
and watch your step.

546
00:21:14,440 --> 00:21:15,920
Do not look at your phone.

547
00:21:16,200 --> 00:21:17,680
Passengers with large luggage

548
00:21:17,680 --> 00:21:19,160
and strollers,

549
00:21:19,640 --> 00:21:21,880
please do not use the escalator.

550
00:21:23,160 --> 00:21:24,310
A suspicious man spotted in the underpass.

551
00:21:24,310 --> 00:21:25,440
Requesting backup.

552
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:26,790
Hold on!

553
00:21:27,350 --> 00:21:27,880
Stop!

554
00:21:27,920 --> 00:21:28,590
Stop there!

555
00:21:28,680 --> 00:21:29,610
Hold on for a sec.

556
00:21:32,270 --> 00:21:34,200
How did you get so much blood on you?

557
00:21:35,680 --> 00:21:37,270
I-I'm a doctor.

558
00:21:37,510 --> 00:21:39,160
I got this blood on me

559
00:21:39,160 --> 00:21:40,350
when delivering a baby.

560
00:21:40,350 --> 00:21:42,510
[Happy New Year]

561
00:21:40,550 --> 00:21:41,480
You're a doctor?

562
00:21:41,590 --> 00:21:42,590
Which hospital do you work in?

563
00:21:42,590 --> 00:21:43,920
Xiaoximen Hospital...

564
00:21:44,790 --> 00:21:46,920
I mean, Fuzhou Kangtaierke Hospital.

565
00:21:47,350 --> 00:21:48,750
You're saying a doctor from Fuzhou

566
00:21:48,750 --> 00:21:49,510
came all the way here

567
00:21:49,510 --> 00:21:50,750
to Bengbu to deliver a baby?

568
00:21:50,750 --> 00:21:51,110
No.

569
00:21:51,310 --> 00:21:52,160
Officer,

570
00:21:52,350 --> 00:21:53,640
it was a rather complicated situation.

571
00:21:53,640 --> 00:21:54,640
A true emergency.

572
00:21:54,680 --> 00:21:56,160
When I was riding a train,

573
00:21:56,510 --> 00:21:57,350
a pregnant woman

574
00:21:57,350 --> 00:21:58,030
was about to give birth,

575
00:21:58,030 --> 00:21:59,630
so I helped deliver the baby.

576
00:22:01,640 --> 00:22:02,790
Do doctors nowadays

577
00:22:02,790 --> 00:22:04,450
not wear white coats anymore?

578
00:22:04,680 --> 00:22:05,720
You got blood all over your coat,

579
00:22:05,720 --> 00:22:06,590
and you didn't even get changed?

580
00:22:06,590 --> 00:22:07,400
Show me your ID now.

581
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:08,240
I wish I could get changed,

582
00:22:08,240 --> 00:22:09,160
but my luggage

583
00:22:09,160 --> 00:22:09,720
and all my stuff

584
00:22:09,720 --> 00:22:10,680
was on that train.

585
00:22:10,680 --> 00:22:11,310
It left.

586
00:22:11,310 --> 00:22:12,830
I'm going to the train station now.

587
00:22:12,830 --> 00:22:13,960
Show me your ID, now!

588
00:22:15,350 --> 00:22:16,160
Fine.

589
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:18,030
P-Please, don't get all worked up.

590
00:22:18,030 --> 00:22:19,030
I'm reaching for it.

591
00:22:19,030 --> 00:22:19,960
I have my ID on me.

592
00:22:22,350 --> 00:22:23,880
Where's my wallet?

593
00:22:24,550 --> 00:22:25,200
Hold still!

594
00:22:25,200 --> 00:22:25,640
No.

595
00:22:25,640 --> 00:22:26,200
Don't move!

596
00:22:26,200 --> 00:22:27,590
-I lost my wallet.
-Halt!

597
00:22:27,590 --> 00:22:28,790
M-My wallet...

598
00:22:28,790 --> 00:22:29,920
My wallet is gone.

599
00:22:29,920 --> 00:22:30,510
My wallet...

600
00:22:30,510 --> 00:22:31,030
Don't move!

601
00:22:31,030 --> 00:22:32,430
My ID is in my wallet!

602
00:22:33,830 --> 00:22:35,200
My ID is in my wallet!

603
00:22:35,400 --> 00:22:37,510
I-I am a good person!

604
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:39,480
I'm a doctor!

605
00:22:39,750 --> 00:22:41,270
I'm calling the police!

606
00:22:40,770 --> 00:22:44,270
[Police]

607
00:22:46,060 --> 00:22:50,170
[Police]

608
00:22:48,440 --> 00:22:49,830
It was truly a mistake.

609
00:22:50,170 --> 00:22:56,360
[Police Duty Office
of Bengbu Railway Station]

610
00:22:50,400 --> 00:22:51,240
A mistake.

611
00:22:51,240 --> 00:22:51,920
Are you sure?

612
00:22:51,920 --> 00:22:52,680
Yes.

613
00:22:52,830 --> 00:22:53,590
They explained to me.

614
00:22:53,590 --> 00:22:54,850
I've sorted it all out.

615
00:22:58,070 --> 00:22:58,880
Mr. Liu,

616
00:23:00,030 --> 00:23:01,400
sorry about what happened.

617
00:23:01,400 --> 00:23:02,330
It was a mistake.

618
00:23:02,640 --> 00:23:04,270
You did do a good deed

619
00:23:04,350 --> 00:23:05,830
and help other passengers.

620
00:23:05,830 --> 00:23:06,350
Yes, yes.

621
00:23:06,350 --> 00:23:08,350
That's why you were thrown off
your schedule.

622
00:23:08,350 --> 00:23:09,640
Our supervisor made an exception

623
00:23:09,640 --> 00:23:10,960
and proposed to buy you

624
00:23:10,960 --> 00:23:12,090
a ticket to Nanjing.

625
00:23:12,110 --> 00:23:12,920
It's free of charge.

626
00:23:12,920 --> 00:23:14,070
Yes, free of charge.

627
00:23:14,070 --> 00:23:15,800
This matter is not about money.

628
00:23:16,480 --> 00:23:18,160
It's not about train tickets either.

629
00:23:18,160 --> 00:23:19,440
Aren't you a police officer?

630
00:23:19,440 --> 00:23:20,970
Just help me find my wallet.

631
00:23:21,030 --> 00:23:21,790
Oh my goodness.

632
00:23:21,790 --> 00:23:22,480
Mr. Liu,

633
00:23:22,480 --> 00:23:23,480
think about it.

634
00:23:23,480 --> 00:23:24,680
Your wallet was left behind in a taxi,

635
00:23:24,680 --> 00:23:26,310
which you hailed randomly on the street.

636
00:23:26,310 --> 00:23:27,270
And you didn't get

637
00:23:27,270 --> 00:23:28,350
a receipt from the driver.

638
00:23:28,350 --> 00:23:29,240
Besides, there's no

639
00:23:29,240 --> 00:23:30,510
electronic payment record.

640
00:23:30,510 --> 00:23:32,570
How am I supposed to find your wallet?

641
00:23:33,510 --> 00:23:34,270
Look at that.

642
00:23:34,270 --> 00:23:35,790
Pull the surveillance footage.

643
00:23:35,790 --> 00:23:36,880
There are surveillance cameras

644
00:23:36,880 --> 00:23:38,400
everywhere, staying on 24/7.

645
00:23:38,400 --> 00:23:39,440
Yeah, right.

646
00:23:39,480 --> 00:23:42,140
But it takes time to find it
through the footage.

647
00:23:42,510 --> 00:23:43,750
How about this?

648
00:23:44,790 --> 00:23:46,480
Leave your contact info with us.

649
00:23:46,480 --> 00:23:47,110
We'll let you know

650
00:23:47,110 --> 00:23:48,570
when your wallet is found.

651
00:23:48,640 --> 00:23:49,440
Is it okay?

652
00:23:50,790 --> 00:23:52,000
That'll work.

653
00:23:55,920 --> 00:23:57,720
Then what about my luggage on the train?

654
00:23:57,720 --> 00:23:58,920
Have you found it yet?

655
00:23:59,160 --> 00:24:00,440
Don't worry about that.

656
00:24:00,440 --> 00:24:01,310
I've confirmed with

657
00:24:01,310 --> 00:24:02,110
the train conductor.

658
00:24:02,110 --> 00:24:02,720
Your mother already

659
00:24:02,720 --> 00:24:03,960
collected your luggage.

660
00:24:03,960 --> 00:24:04,750
Who?

661
00:24:04,960 --> 00:24:05,880
Your mother.

662
00:24:10,790 --> 00:24:11,590
My mother...

663
00:24:13,310 --> 00:24:14,240
She passed long ago.

664
00:24:14,240 --> 00:24:16,110
How could she have collected my luggage?

665
00:24:16,110 --> 00:24:17,920
W-What kind of confirmation is that?

666
00:24:17,920 --> 00:24:18,680
But

667
00:24:18,680 --> 00:24:20,240
this is what I was told.

668
00:24:20,240 --> 00:24:20,920
Look.

669
00:24:21,440 --> 00:24:23,110
It's a woman in her sixties,

670
00:24:23,110 --> 00:24:23,680
who

671
00:24:23,680 --> 00:24:24,960
shared a bunk with you.

672
00:24:25,240 --> 00:24:26,440
I don't know her.

673
00:24:26,440 --> 00:24:27,640
She's not my mother.

674
00:24:30,030 --> 00:24:31,160
What a mess.

675
00:24:31,640 --> 00:24:33,160
Maybe she was just being nice and offered

676
00:24:33,160 --> 00:24:34,440
to watch over your stuff.

677
00:24:34,440 --> 00:24:34,750
Yeah.

678
00:24:34,750 --> 00:24:35,400
Think hard.

679
00:24:35,400 --> 00:24:36,270
Perhaps there was

680
00:24:36,270 --> 00:24:37,590
some sort of mistake.

681
00:24:39,480 --> 00:24:40,110
Don't fret.

682
00:24:40,110 --> 00:24:41,160
Don't worry.

683
00:24:41,310 --> 00:24:43,030
Yeah, think about it carefully.

684
00:24:43,030 --> 00:24:43,880
Officers,

685
00:24:44,070 --> 00:24:45,680
I'm not fretting.

686
00:24:46,240 --> 00:24:47,070
It's just that my luggage

687
00:24:47,070 --> 00:24:48,270
is really important.

688
00:24:48,830 --> 00:24:49,790
Sorry.

689
00:24:49,790 --> 00:24:51,120
We're not of help to you.

690
00:24:51,350 --> 00:24:52,790
But we'll try to get in contact

691
00:24:52,790 --> 00:24:55,120
with this older woman as soon as possible.

692
00:24:56,590 --> 00:24:57,310
How about this?

693
00:24:57,310 --> 00:24:58,110
You buy me a ticket

694
00:24:58,110 --> 00:24:59,350
to Fuzhou.

695
00:24:59,920 --> 00:25:01,030
When the luggage is retrieved,

696
00:25:01,030 --> 00:25:02,030
send it to me.

697
00:25:02,720 --> 00:25:03,400
Then...

698
00:25:03,400 --> 00:25:05,060
when would you like to set out?

699
00:25:06,550 --> 00:25:08,310
Someone will pick me up in Fuzhou.

700
00:25:08,310 --> 00:25:08,920
B-But I...

701
00:25:08,920 --> 00:25:09,920
I need to ask them

702
00:25:10,240 --> 00:25:10,920
about the exact time.

703
00:25:10,920 --> 00:25:11,850
I'll make a call.

704
00:25:12,270 --> 00:25:12,880
Okay.

705
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:14,270
Alright. I'll make the call outside.

706
00:25:14,270 --> 00:25:15,730
Just don't worry, Mr. Liu.

707
00:25:17,070 --> 00:25:17,720
What went wrong?

708
00:25:17,720 --> 00:25:18,590
His mother is dead.

709
00:25:18,590 --> 00:25:20,390
Who told you she got his luggage?

710
00:25:28,350 --> 00:25:29,270
Who's calling?

711
00:25:30,110 --> 00:25:30,790
A doctor

712
00:25:30,790 --> 00:25:32,200
who's on his way to join us.

713
00:25:32,200 --> 00:25:33,160
In fact, I don't know him.

714
00:25:33,160 --> 00:25:34,550
It's President Hong's arrangement.

715
00:25:34,550 --> 00:25:35,550
Answer the phone.

716
00:25:35,640 --> 00:25:36,350
Put it on speaker.

717
00:25:36,350 --> 00:25:37,000
Okay.

718
00:25:39,440 --> 00:25:40,110
Hello?

719
00:25:40,590 --> 00:25:41,720
Secretary Ni?

720
00:25:42,160 --> 00:25:42,830
It's me.

721
00:25:42,920 --> 00:25:44,400
I'm Liu Zhengliang.

722
00:25:44,880 --> 00:25:45,750
We talked to each other

723
00:25:45,750 --> 00:25:46,720
previously.

724
00:25:46,920 --> 00:25:47,880
I'm the doctor coming from

725
00:25:47,880 --> 00:25:49,350
the Northeast to join the hospital.

726
00:25:49,350 --> 00:25:50,240
I remember you.

727
00:25:50,240 --> 00:25:51,640
You're arriving tomorrow, right?

728
00:25:51,520 --> 00:25:58,730
[Happy New Year]

729
00:25:51,640 --> 00:25:52,270
Yes.

730
00:25:52,680 --> 00:25:54,270
I was just getting to that.

731
00:25:54,480 --> 00:25:55,400
Well, I...

732
00:25:55,790 --> 00:25:56,590
I...

733
00:25:56,830 --> 00:25:57,960
I had a little problem on the way.

734
00:25:57,960 --> 00:25:59,890
Now, I'm officially informing you

735
00:25:59,960 --> 00:26:01,110
that you don't need to come here.

736
00:26:01,110 --> 00:26:01,960
Yeah, right.

737
00:26:02,070 --> 00:26:02,750
I don't think

738
00:26:02,750 --> 00:26:04,200
I can reach the hospital tomorrow.

739
00:26:04,200 --> 00:26:05,000
I guess I won't

740
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:06,160
be there until the day

741
00:26:06,160 --> 00:26:07,750
after tomorrow at the earliest.

742
00:26:07,750 --> 00:26:08,480
No, no, no.

743
00:26:08,510 --> 00:26:09,720
I mean

744
00:26:09,750 --> 00:26:11,070
you don't need to come

745
00:26:11,070 --> 00:26:12,160
to Fuzhou at all.

746
00:26:13,550 --> 00:26:14,480
What's that now?

747
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:16,200
It was Hong Bin who told you

748
00:26:16,200 --> 00:26:17,240
to come for a visit

749
00:26:17,240 --> 00:26:18,640
and join the crew, right?

750
00:26:20,440 --> 00:26:22,000
I was recommended

751
00:26:22,030 --> 00:26:23,400
by my former supervisor.

752
00:26:23,400 --> 00:26:24,510
He said President Hong

753
00:26:24,510 --> 00:26:25,680
was a school mate of his.

754
00:26:25,680 --> 00:26:27,480
Hong Bin is now under investigation

755
00:26:27,480 --> 00:26:28,350
for suspected

756
00:26:28,680 --> 00:26:30,270
embezzlement and accepting bribes.

757
00:26:30,270 --> 00:26:31,640
He is no longer the president

758
00:26:31,640 --> 00:26:32,570
of our hospital.

759
00:26:33,270 --> 00:26:33,920
And now

760
00:26:33,920 --> 00:26:35,440
we can't offer you a job.

761
00:26:35,440 --> 00:26:35,880
So

762
00:26:35,880 --> 00:26:37,070
you'll have to try your luck

763
00:26:37,070 --> 00:26:37,830
with another hospital.

764
00:26:37,830 --> 00:26:38,200
No, no.

765
00:26:38,200 --> 00:26:39,440
Wait a minute. Wait.

766
00:26:40,750 --> 00:26:42,150
Let me comb this through.

767
00:26:42,640 --> 00:26:43,640
Let me sort it out.

768
00:26:46,160 --> 00:26:46,960
Secretary Ni.

769
00:26:47,960 --> 00:26:48,750
Listen,

770
00:26:49,270 --> 00:26:51,030
I set out from the Northeast.

771
00:26:51,510 --> 00:26:53,440
I've been on the train for two days.

772
00:26:53,750 --> 00:26:54,920
At the moment, I'm in a bind

773
00:26:54,920 --> 00:26:56,250
and stranded in Bengbu.

774
00:26:56,270 --> 00:26:57,070
All my luggage

775
00:26:57,070 --> 00:26:58,510
is on the previous train.

776
00:26:58,510 --> 00:26:59,310
Thank you for calling.

777
00:26:59,310 --> 00:27:00,680
Have a nice trip then.

778
00:27:00,680 --> 00:27:02,030
What nice trip?

779
00:27:02,030 --> 00:27:03,160
There's nothing...

780
00:27:04,640 --> 00:27:06,030
Mr. Liu! Mr. Liu.

781
00:27:06,310 --> 00:27:07,070
I spoke

782
00:27:07,070 --> 00:27:08,200
with my supervisor.

783
00:27:08,200 --> 00:27:09,310
He agreed to buy you

784
00:27:09,310 --> 00:27:10,440
a ticket to Fuzhou.

785
00:27:10,640 --> 00:27:12,300
When would you like to set out?

786
00:27:12,790 --> 00:27:13,310
No.

787
00:27:13,350 --> 00:27:15,010
Well, can you give me a second?

788
00:27:15,310 --> 00:27:16,570
Things are a bit messy.

789
00:27:17,070 --> 00:27:18,790
I-I need to sort them out.

790
00:27:18,790 --> 00:27:19,480
Look,

791
00:27:19,750 --> 00:27:20,790
I'll make one more call.

792
00:27:20,790 --> 00:27:21,720
Give me a moment.

793
00:27:21,760 --> 00:27:23,970
[Conference Room]

794
00:27:24,160 --> 00:27:26,860
[Liu Zhengliang]

795
00:27:26,940 --> 00:27:31,550
[Healing pain with compassion,
lighting up hope with dedication]

796
00:27:28,350 --> 00:27:29,200
Well done!

797
00:27:29,790 --> 00:27:31,270
That caught me off guard.

798
00:27:32,920 --> 00:27:34,320
Please dial again later.

799
00:27:35,320 --> 00:27:37,820
[Police Office of Bengbu Railway Station]

800
00:27:40,550 --> 00:27:42,690
[Police]

801
00:27:43,070 --> 00:27:43,920
Good job!

802
00:27:45,070 --> 00:27:46,200
That was a topspin loop.

803
00:27:46,200 --> 00:27:47,070
[Liu Zhengliang]

804
00:27:47,420 --> 00:27:49,870
[Missed call] [Liu Zhengliang]

805
00:27:49,930 --> 00:27:54,760
[Police]

806
00:27:54,720 --> 00:27:56,350
That smash you did looked just like

807
00:27:54,840 --> 00:28:04,620
[Healing pain with compassion,
lighting up hope with dedication]

808
00:27:56,350 --> 00:27:57,030
Ma Long's.

809
00:27:57,160 --> 00:27:57,790
I'm exhausted.

810
00:27:57,790 --> 00:27:58,830
D-Drink this.

811
00:27:58,830 --> 00:27:59,510
No, I'd rather not.

812
00:27:59,510 --> 00:28:00,270
After exercise,

813
00:28:00,270 --> 00:28:01,200
you should drink this.

814
00:28:01,200 --> 00:28:01,640
Let me wipe my sweat.

815
00:28:01,640 --> 00:28:03,370
It replenishes electrolytes.

816
00:28:04,590 --> 00:28:05,400
Oh you.

817
00:28:05,510 --> 00:28:07,710
You don't have to let me win every point.

818
00:28:07,830 --> 00:28:08,590
I d-didn't...

819
00:28:08,590 --> 00:28:10,070
So you saw it through?

820
00:28:10,440 --> 00:28:11,900
I didn't really hold back.

821
00:28:11,920 --> 00:28:13,000
I certainly saw it through.

822
00:28:13,000 --> 00:28:15,200
Or your efforts would be in vain, right?

823
00:28:15,350 --> 00:28:17,200
I just wanted to cheer you up.

824
00:28:17,510 --> 00:28:18,270
You've been working

825
00:28:18,270 --> 00:28:19,920
hard and under too much pressure.

826
00:28:19,920 --> 00:28:21,000
You need to relax.

827
00:28:21,030 --> 00:28:22,830
Why would you want to cheer me up?

828
00:28:23,310 --> 00:28:24,110
You were pleasing me.

829
00:28:24,110 --> 00:28:25,640
What is your real purpose?

830
00:28:25,640 --> 00:28:26,240
No, nothing.

831
00:28:26,240 --> 00:28:27,110
You want to be the vice president?

832
00:28:27,110 --> 00:28:27,830
No, I don't.

833
00:28:27,830 --> 00:28:29,110
I'm not qualified for it.

834
00:28:29,110 --> 00:28:29,920
I'm not.

835
00:28:32,790 --> 00:28:33,880
You're up for the job.

836
00:28:33,880 --> 00:28:34,830
I am not.

837
00:28:34,830 --> 00:28:35,510
I'm absolutely not.

838
00:28:35,510 --> 00:28:37,040
I'm sure you'll do a good job

839
00:28:37,270 --> 00:28:38,350
If you take the position.

840
00:28:38,350 --> 00:28:39,510
No, I'm not up for it.

841
00:28:39,550 --> 00:28:40,830
You're best suited to play

842
00:28:40,830 --> 00:28:42,240
the role of the wise leader.

843
00:28:42,240 --> 00:28:43,030
You are meant

844
00:28:43,070 --> 00:28:43,960
to be the leader.

845
00:28:43,960 --> 00:28:45,090
I'm feeling so good.

846
00:28:45,680 --> 00:28:46,790
Get me my coat.

847
00:28:47,480 --> 00:28:48,920
I'm sweating all over.
Better not catch a cold.

848
00:28:48,920 --> 00:28:49,790
That's right.

849
00:28:50,960 --> 00:28:52,490
You've really worked hard.

850
00:28:53,550 --> 00:28:55,030
Let me give you a massage.

851
00:28:57,030 --> 00:28:58,160
In such a short while,

852
00:28:58,160 --> 00:28:59,690
I missed more than 10 calls.

853
00:29:02,510 --> 00:29:03,880
Guess who made them.

854
00:29:04,510 --> 00:29:05,310
I...

855
00:29:05,440 --> 00:29:06,110
Definitely

856
00:29:06,110 --> 00:29:07,240
not your wife.

857
00:29:07,750 --> 00:29:08,640
If it were her,

858
00:29:08,640 --> 00:29:09,970
you wouldn't be so calm.

859
00:29:11,200 --> 00:29:12,400
It's Liu Zhengliang.

860
00:29:13,880 --> 00:29:14,590
What's with him?

861
00:29:14,590 --> 00:29:16,390
Why did he give you so many calls?

862
00:29:18,160 --> 00:29:19,360
I'm calling him back.

863
00:29:20,720 --> 00:29:21,720
I-I-I am

864
00:29:22,070 --> 00:29:22,870
leaving then.

865
00:29:31,530 --> 00:29:37,430
[Police Office of Bengbu Railway Station]

866
00:29:37,030 --> 00:29:37,550
Hello.

867
00:29:37,920 --> 00:29:39,920
You called me, didn't you?

868
00:29:40,320 --> 00:29:44,750
[Police]

869
00:29:40,440 --> 00:29:42,170
The hospital you referred me to

870
00:29:42,440 --> 00:29:43,480
won't hire me now.

871
00:29:43,720 --> 00:29:44,720
What should I do?

872
00:29:45,160 --> 00:29:46,220
Who won't hire you?

873
00:29:46,550 --> 00:29:48,680
Just the person you told me to contact.

874
00:29:50,550 --> 00:29:51,550
You mean Hong Bin?

875
00:29:52,240 --> 00:29:53,790
No, his secretary.

876
00:29:54,270 --> 00:29:55,400
This man said Hong Bin was arrested

877
00:29:55,400 --> 00:29:56,110
for corruption and bribery.

878
00:29:56,110 --> 00:29:57,110
Really?

879
00:29:58,640 --> 00:29:59,970
What should you do then?

880
00:30:01,030 --> 00:30:02,110
You're asking me?

881
00:30:02,640 --> 00:30:04,200
I should be the one asking you.

882
00:30:04,200 --> 00:30:05,270
How could you introduce someone

883
00:30:05,270 --> 00:30:06,400
so unreliable to me?

884
00:30:08,200 --> 00:30:09,000
Wait.

885
00:30:09,720 --> 00:30:10,510
You see,

886
00:30:11,720 --> 00:30:14,240
there was never a problem
throughout Hong Bin's

887
00:30:14,240 --> 00:30:14,880
career.

888
00:30:14,880 --> 00:30:15,680
But the moment

889
00:30:16,110 --> 00:30:17,110
you showed up, he was

890
00:30:17,060 --> 00:30:21,320
[Police]

891
00:30:17,110 --> 00:30:18,550
brought down abruptly. How come?

892
00:30:18,550 --> 00:30:19,880
What do you mean by that?

893
00:30:19,920 --> 00:30:21,440
Are you saying this is my fault?

894
00:30:21,440 --> 00:30:22,350
No, it's not your fault.

895
00:30:22,350 --> 00:30:23,590
I'm just concerned and worried

896
00:30:23,590 --> 00:30:24,680
about you, aren't I?

897
00:30:24,680 --> 00:30:26,000
Cut the crap.

898
00:30:24,850 --> 00:30:32,890
[Police]

899
00:30:26,550 --> 00:30:27,750
I'm telling you, I...

900
00:30:28,440 --> 00:30:30,110
I'm in an awkward situation now.

901
00:30:30,110 --> 00:30:31,770
Utterly and sheerly awkward.

902
00:30:31,880 --> 00:30:33,240
You have to take full responsibility,
don't you?

903
00:30:33,240 --> 00:30:35,510
Full responsibility? Why is it all on me?

904
00:30:36,110 --> 00:30:36,960
How about this?

905
00:30:36,960 --> 00:30:38,310
Just come back here.

906
00:30:39,550 --> 00:30:42,810
[Police]

907
00:30:39,590 --> 00:30:41,310
I'm not going back, I'm telling you.

908
00:30:41,310 --> 00:30:43,070
I'd sooner be dead than back there.

909
00:30:43,070 --> 00:30:44,960
At worst, I'll just find a job right here.

910
00:30:44,960 --> 00:30:45,590
You think

911
00:30:45,590 --> 00:30:46,990
I can't find a job or what?

912
00:30:47,480 --> 00:30:48,610
Oh, Liu Zhengliang.

913
00:30:50,510 --> 00:30:51,240
Mr. Liu,

914
00:30:51,350 --> 00:30:51,960
I got you

915
00:30:51,960 --> 00:30:52,590
a coat of mine.

916
00:30:52,590 --> 00:30:53,720
Why not get changed?

917
00:30:58,070 --> 00:30:58,960
Mr. Liu.

918
00:30:59,590 --> 00:31:01,510
No need to smell it. It's been washed.

919
00:31:01,510 --> 00:31:02,310
Mr. Liu.

920
00:31:03,480 --> 00:31:04,270
Have you decided

921
00:31:04,270 --> 00:31:05,200
when to leave?

922
00:31:09,640 --> 00:31:11,640
I-I am still waiting for your reply.

923
00:31:14,680 --> 00:31:15,790
It sounded to me that Liu Zhengliang

924
00:31:15,790 --> 00:31:16,550
got a problem

925
00:31:16,550 --> 00:31:17,750
out there, didn't he?

926
00:31:17,960 --> 00:31:18,760
It's my fault.

927
00:31:19,750 --> 00:31:21,350
I referred him to a hospital,

928
00:31:21,350 --> 00:31:23,010
but it later ran into trouble.

929
00:31:24,270 --> 00:31:25,000
Then what to do with it?

930
00:31:25,000 --> 00:31:26,350
We must quickly come up with a solution.

931
00:31:26,350 --> 00:31:26,790
Talk him into...

932
00:31:26,790 --> 00:31:27,850
Talk him into what?

933
00:31:28,350 --> 00:31:29,680
He refused to come back.

934
00:31:29,750 --> 00:31:30,880
Didn't you just ask him

935
00:31:30,880 --> 00:31:32,070
to come back here?

936
00:31:32,070 --> 00:31:32,880
He should come back.

937
00:31:32,880 --> 00:31:33,640
Our hospital is great.

938
00:31:33,640 --> 00:31:35,300
These things can't be forced.

939
00:31:35,440 --> 00:31:36,480
We are already

940
00:31:36,480 --> 00:31:37,680
in trouble ourselves.

941
00:31:37,680 --> 00:31:39,410
How are we supposed to help him?

942
00:31:43,310 --> 00:31:44,000
During

943
00:31:44,480 --> 00:31:46,000
t-the meeting on Monday,

944
00:31:46,000 --> 00:31:48,730
did someone propose
to disband Xiaoximen again?

945
00:31:52,240 --> 00:31:53,640
They are the knife,

946
00:31:53,920 --> 00:31:54,720
but I, Long Dongdong, am

947
00:31:54,720 --> 00:31:56,310
no chopping block.

948
00:32:05,200 --> 00:32:06,400
Eat it while it's hot.

949
00:32:14,440 --> 00:32:15,370
Coming right up!

950
00:32:18,030 --> 00:32:18,830
Who is it?

951
00:32:22,550 --> 00:32:23,750
Why did you come here?

952
00:32:24,310 --> 00:32:25,590
I brought you two something extra

953
00:32:25,590 --> 00:32:26,510
to eat—a pizza.

954
00:32:27,510 --> 00:32:28,720
Well, this is not a good time.

955
00:32:28,720 --> 00:32:29,400
Why don't you

956
00:32:29,400 --> 00:32:30,240
keep it for yourself?

957
00:32:30,240 --> 00:32:31,830
Comrade Changhai. Comrade Changhai!

958
00:32:31,830 --> 00:32:33,350
-Take it back and share it with others.
-Do you remember me?

959
00:32:33,350 --> 00:32:34,410
Comrade Changhai?

960
00:32:35,400 --> 00:32:36,530
Commissioner Chen.

961
00:32:37,550 --> 00:32:38,350
I waited a long time for you.

962
00:32:38,350 --> 00:32:40,200
-Let's go inside.
-Better eat this while it's hot!

963
00:32:40,200 --> 00:32:40,920
Did you have a safe journey?

964
00:32:40,920 --> 00:32:41,830
Yes, very safe.

965
00:32:41,830 --> 00:32:43,240
-Hello.
-No one was tailing you, right?

966
00:32:43,240 --> 00:32:43,750
No one.

967
00:32:43,830 --> 00:32:44,510
Don't you worry.

968
00:32:44,510 --> 00:32:44,790
Good.

969
00:32:44,790 --> 00:32:46,450
Everything's well arranged.

970
00:32:47,680 --> 00:32:48,550
You even brought something over.

971
00:32:48,550 --> 00:32:49,750
Oh, look at this.

972
00:32:51,030 --> 00:32:52,640
How did you know I enjoy pizza?

973
00:32:52,640 --> 00:32:53,480
Because it's tasty.

974
00:32:53,480 --> 00:32:54,810
Mingming enjoys it too.

975
00:32:57,640 --> 00:32:58,680
So much cheese.

976
00:32:59,960 --> 00:33:01,960
To keep up with the fast pace of life,

977
00:33:02,030 --> 00:33:04,200
urban residents like to

978
00:33:04,880 --> 00:33:06,010
fill their stomachs

979
00:33:06,070 --> 00:33:07,680
with highly processed food like this.

980
00:33:07,680 --> 00:33:09,010
It's not healthy at all.

981
00:33:09,270 --> 00:33:11,510
-Awful.
-If you can't stand it, just leave.

982
00:33:11,510 --> 00:33:12,920
No, bro, you don't get it.

983
00:33:12,960 --> 00:33:13,830
Some people like

984
00:33:13,830 --> 00:33:15,400
to wrap the meat filling inside,

985
00:33:15,400 --> 00:33:16,440
but Uncle Che here

986
00:33:16,880 --> 00:33:18,590
likes the meat filling to show.

987
00:33:18,590 --> 00:33:19,750
It's chewy in the mouth,

988
00:33:19,750 --> 00:33:21,070
and smells good on the outside.

989
00:33:21,070 --> 00:33:22,030
Delicious, isn't it?

990
00:33:22,030 --> 00:33:22,510
Yes, it is.

991
00:33:22,510 --> 00:33:23,960
I noticed that last time

992
00:33:23,960 --> 00:33:24,720
I ate it.

993
00:33:24,720 --> 00:33:25,510
Oh, you.

994
00:33:26,480 --> 00:33:27,270
Have some more if you think

995
00:33:27,270 --> 00:33:27,870
it's good.

996
00:33:28,030 --> 00:33:30,640
We used to be married,
and that left us a lasting bond.

997
00:33:30,640 --> 00:33:32,000
Now, I have found

998
00:33:32,000 --> 00:33:33,400
the true meaning of life.

999
00:33:33,640 --> 00:33:35,240
I have the obligation, the responsibility,

1000
00:33:35,240 --> 00:33:36,160
and the capability

1001
00:33:36,160 --> 00:33:38,220
to get you out of misery along with me.

1002
00:33:41,240 --> 00:33:42,790
You're choking. Don't eat so fast.

1003
00:33:42,790 --> 00:33:44,000
If you can't stand it either,

1004
00:33:44,000 --> 00:33:44,790
just leave.

1005
00:33:46,000 --> 00:33:47,830
I choked on my own saliva.

1006
00:33:47,830 --> 00:33:48,720
I just chocked.

1007
00:33:50,110 --> 00:33:51,240
Get me some tissues.

1008
00:33:52,200 --> 00:33:54,460
How about you stay in the room
for a while?

1009
00:33:55,680 --> 00:33:56,810
Commissioner Chen.

1010
00:33:57,200 --> 00:33:57,880
I don't think

1011
00:33:57,880 --> 00:33:59,070
this is a good place to talk.

1012
00:33:59,070 --> 00:33:59,680
It is high time

1013
00:33:59,680 --> 00:34:01,280
we changed our meeting spot.

1014
00:34:01,510 --> 00:34:02,640
Uncle Che, no rush.

1015
00:34:03,030 --> 00:34:03,750
Wait a moment.

1016
00:34:03,750 --> 00:34:05,010
Wait a moment for what?

1017
00:34:05,200 --> 00:34:06,030
Aren't you here

1018
00:34:06,030 --> 00:34:07,560
to meet my father in secret?

1019
00:34:09,550 --> 00:34:10,360
Uncle Che.

1020
00:34:11,320 --> 00:34:12,510
Time to change the meeting spot.

1021
00:34:12,510 --> 00:34:13,150
Let's go.

1022
00:34:13,190 --> 00:34:13,840
A change now?

1023
00:34:13,840 --> 00:34:14,570
A change now.

1024
00:34:15,880 --> 00:34:16,670
T-This...

1025
00:34:16,670 --> 00:34:17,320
Eat it in the room.

1026
00:34:17,320 --> 00:34:18,000
Won't you have a piece?

1027
00:34:18,000 --> 00:34:18,480
No, no.

1028
00:34:18,480 --> 00:34:19,070
Let's go.

1029
00:34:20,670 --> 00:34:21,190
Where?

1030
00:34:21,190 --> 00:34:22,150
Here, this way.

1031
00:34:22,639 --> 00:34:23,880
[Restricted area;
Authorized personnel only]

1032
00:34:25,920 --> 00:34:26,380
Come on.

1033
00:34:29,320 --> 00:34:30,580
In light of the current

1034
00:34:30,920 --> 00:34:31,980
urgent situation,

1035
00:34:32,320 --> 00:34:33,840
we must send a distress signal

1036
00:34:33,840 --> 00:34:34,840
to the headquarters.

1037
00:34:34,840 --> 00:34:35,770
Tell me about it.

1038
00:34:35,960 --> 00:34:38,489
Signal three short, three long,
three short.

1039
00:34:38,510 --> 00:34:39,639
What does that mean?

1040
00:34:42,190 --> 00:34:42,790
Mingming.

1041
00:34:44,800 --> 00:34:46,440
I've planned it all out.

1042
00:34:47,360 --> 00:34:48,440
Listen to me.

1043
00:34:49,630 --> 00:34:51,400
Sell this house first.

1044
00:34:51,710 --> 00:34:53,510
Then we'll build new ones there.

1045
00:34:53,510 --> 00:34:54,320
The three of us will raise

1046
00:34:54,320 --> 00:34:55,840
seven or eight reindeer on the mountain.

1047
00:34:55,840 --> 00:34:57,590
I'll open a small clinic
at the mountain foot.

1048
00:34:57,590 --> 00:34:58,840
We'll buy a pickup truck

1049
00:34:58,140 --> 00:35:02,070
[Restricted area;
Authorized personnel only]

1050
00:34:59,190 --> 00:35:00,840
to transport goods for the villagers.

1051
00:35:00,840 --> 00:35:03,030
A life of comfort and respect
is awaiting us.

1052
00:35:03,030 --> 00:35:04,840
Let's bid a final farewell
to inner friction

1053
00:35:04,840 --> 00:35:06,110
and all the hustle and bustle.

1054
00:35:06,110 --> 00:35:06,960
Your father...

1055
00:35:06,960 --> 00:35:07,960
Our father

1056
00:35:07,960 --> 00:35:09,320
might be cured there.

1057
00:35:09,630 --> 00:35:10,760
Can you picture it?

1058
00:35:11,590 --> 00:35:12,230
When we get there,

1059
00:35:12,230 --> 00:35:13,230
you won't have to work at all.

1060
00:35:13,230 --> 00:35:14,670
I'll chop wood, make fires, and cook.

1061
00:35:14,670 --> 00:35:16,200
All the chores will be mine.

1062
00:35:18,070 --> 00:35:18,880
Hao,

1063
00:35:20,190 --> 00:35:22,400
we're already divorced.

1064
00:35:22,840 --> 00:35:24,670
You and I have nothing to do
with each other.

1065
00:35:24,670 --> 00:35:25,230
You just

1066
00:35:25,230 --> 00:35:27,110
live your life well.

1067
00:35:27,400 --> 00:35:28,880
And I'll be truly happy for you.

1068
00:35:28,880 --> 00:35:30,440
You don't need to worry
about me and my father.

1069
00:35:30,440 --> 00:35:31,030
Okay?

1070
00:35:31,050 --> 00:35:32,690
But you have to believe me.

1071
00:35:33,550 --> 00:35:36,030
What you're living now is not a real life.

1072
00:35:36,030 --> 00:35:36,840
You are...

1073
00:35:37,000 --> 00:35:39,840
You are just making do with reality.

1074
00:35:49,360 --> 00:35:50,150
Yes.

1075
00:35:50,920 --> 00:35:52,400
My life is not that great.

1076
00:35:52,510 --> 00:35:53,480
I have to work.

1077
00:35:53,800 --> 00:35:54,930
I have to make money.

1078
00:35:55,190 --> 00:35:57,110
And I have to take care of my father.

1079
00:35:57,110 --> 00:35:58,640
The one and only dream I have

1080
00:35:58,920 --> 00:36:00,120
is to get a doctorate.

1081
00:36:00,800 --> 00:36:02,600
But I can't find a chance to do so.

1082
00:36:03,960 --> 00:36:05,560
Honestly, I really envy you.

1083
00:36:07,440 --> 00:36:08,510
You can go anywhere

1084
00:36:08,880 --> 00:36:10,190
and do anything you want.

1085
00:36:10,190 --> 00:36:11,650
So free and unrestrained.

1086
00:36:11,670 --> 00:36:13,470
It's very brave of you to forsake

1087
00:36:14,150 --> 00:36:15,550
everything for freedom.

1088
00:36:17,800 --> 00:36:18,590
But I...

1089
00:36:19,190 --> 00:36:20,840
I choose to face reality

1090
00:36:22,710 --> 00:36:24,440
and shoulder responsibility.

1091
00:36:24,440 --> 00:36:26,320
I'm still attempting to fight for

1092
00:36:26,320 --> 00:36:27,720
the dream I started with.

1093
00:36:28,230 --> 00:36:29,440
I'm also very brave,

1094
00:36:30,150 --> 00:36:30,760
aren't I?

1095
00:36:32,510 --> 00:36:34,110
Everyone has their own fate.

1096
00:36:34,510 --> 00:36:35,320
It's already

1097
00:36:35,480 --> 00:36:36,880
enough for us to live

1098
00:36:36,880 --> 00:36:37,920
our current lives

1099
00:36:38,320 --> 00:36:38,920
to the fullest.

1100
00:36:38,920 --> 00:36:40,720
No one needs to convince anyone.

1101
00:36:44,150 --> 00:36:44,960
Good.

1102
00:36:45,670 --> 00:36:46,760
Well said.

1103
00:36:47,840 --> 00:36:48,710
Mingming.

1104
00:36:49,880 --> 00:36:51,410
-You're awesome.
-No, bro.

1105
00:36:51,590 --> 00:36:53,320
What do you have to do with this?

1106
00:36:53,800 --> 00:36:54,800
That's not a nice thing to say.

1107
00:36:54,800 --> 00:36:56,230
You have no idea what's going on.

1108
00:36:56,230 --> 00:36:57,360
Please be polite to him.

1109
00:36:57,360 --> 00:36:58,890
He's a co-worker in my unit.

1110
00:36:59,630 --> 00:37:00,440
Your unit?

1111
00:37:00,630 --> 00:37:01,230
Yes.

1112
00:37:01,630 --> 00:37:02,360
What unit?

1113
00:37:02,360 --> 00:37:03,420
A classified unit.

1114
00:37:04,480 --> 00:37:05,960
He was sent by Comrade Xiaobo

1115
00:37:05,960 --> 00:37:08,110
to supervise and protect me.

1116
00:37:08,110 --> 00:37:09,550
He's responsible for my safety.

1117
00:37:09,550 --> 00:37:10,480
Comrade Changhai,

1118
00:37:10,480 --> 00:37:12,150
the organization is not supervising you

1119
00:37:12,150 --> 00:37:14,150
and it trusts you unconditionally.

1120
00:37:14,710 --> 00:37:15,760
I've checked.

1121
00:37:16,190 --> 00:37:17,190
It's not serious.

1122
00:37:17,760 --> 00:37:19,160
Let's resort to surgery.

1123
00:37:19,360 --> 00:37:20,150
Doctor,

1124
00:37:21,130 --> 00:37:22,550
can I not undergo surgery?

1125
00:37:22,550 --> 00:37:24,680
You can just prescribe some medicine.

1126
00:37:26,230 --> 00:37:27,800
Given the current condition,

1127
00:37:27,800 --> 00:37:29,800
conservative treatment is possible.

1128
00:37:29,800 --> 00:37:31,110
But there is a severe narrowing

1129
00:37:31,110 --> 00:37:32,440
in your carotid artery.

1130
00:37:32,510 --> 00:37:33,910
Do you see it? Right here.

1131
00:37:34,360 --> 00:37:35,440
So I still suggest surgery.

1132
00:37:35,440 --> 00:37:36,590
Otherwise, you'll face

1133
00:37:36,590 --> 00:37:38,670
a high risk of cerebral infarction.

1134
00:37:38,800 --> 00:37:39,930
Then the surgery fee

1135
00:37:40,630 --> 00:37:41,440
must be high, right?

1136
00:37:41,440 --> 00:37:43,840
This kind of surgery
is covered by medical insurance.

1137
00:37:43,840 --> 00:37:47,300
After reimbursement, you won't have to
pay much out of pocket.

1138
00:37:47,440 --> 00:37:49,070
Doctor, you have no idea.

1139
00:37:49,280 --> 00:37:51,190
My son doesn't treat me well.

1140
00:37:51,400 --> 00:37:53,070
I don't want to trouble him and his wife.

1141
00:37:53,070 --> 00:37:54,400
Or my daughter-in-law

1142
00:37:54,400 --> 00:37:55,960
will accuse me of being a burden.

1143
00:37:55,960 --> 00:37:57,420
What you said is not right.

1144
00:37:59,630 --> 00:38:01,070
Who do we live for?

1145
00:38:02,150 --> 00:38:03,400
We live for ourselves,

1146
00:38:03,400 --> 00:38:04,710
not our children.

1147
00:38:04,710 --> 00:38:05,400
Yes.

1148
00:38:06,280 --> 00:38:09,010
You were so cool
when you gave that little speech.

1149
00:38:09,110 --> 00:38:10,230
I was moved.

1150
00:38:12,480 --> 00:38:13,440
Focus on the driving.

1151
00:38:13,440 --> 00:38:14,840
Your car's over the line.

1152
00:38:14,920 --> 00:38:15,980
Just a dashed line.

1153
00:38:25,710 --> 00:38:26,970
Chief Physician Tong.

1154
00:38:29,880 --> 00:38:31,190
Okay, I'll tell him.

1155
00:38:32,880 --> 00:38:34,360
Got it. Alright. Bye.

1156
00:38:36,670 --> 00:38:37,230
Next Monday,

1157
00:38:37,230 --> 00:38:38,550
Chief Physician Tong
will perform a surgery.

1158
00:38:38,550 --> 00:38:40,670
He asked me to be the first assistant
and you the second.

1159
00:38:40,670 --> 00:38:42,400
I'll talk to the patient later.

1160
00:38:42,550 --> 00:38:43,630
Me taking part in surgery?

1161
00:38:43,630 --> 00:38:44,960
There must be a mistake.

1162
00:38:46,440 --> 00:38:47,550
Is there any other surgeon

1163
00:38:47,550 --> 00:38:48,800
in our hospital named Chen Junnan?

1164
00:38:48,800 --> 00:38:50,000
What kind of surgery?

1165
00:38:50,000 --> 00:38:51,280
Am I up for it?

1166
00:38:51,880 --> 00:38:54,510
CAS, carotid artery stenting.

1167
00:38:54,710 --> 00:38:55,840
It's not difficult.

1168
00:38:55,920 --> 00:38:58,180
Even an intern can be a second assistant.

1169
00:38:59,360 --> 00:39:01,190
What? Anything wrong?

1170
00:39:01,190 --> 00:39:02,360
Then pick an intern instead.

1171
00:39:02,360 --> 00:39:03,230
Tell Chief Physician Tong

1172
00:39:03,230 --> 00:39:04,030
not to put me on.

1173
00:39:04,030 --> 00:39:05,430
Say that to him yourself.

1174
00:39:06,630 --> 00:39:07,590
Anyway, I heard

1175
00:39:08,150 --> 00:39:09,710
Chief Physician Tong doesn't like you.

1176
00:39:09,710 --> 00:39:11,880
He's looking for an excuse
to get rid of you.

1177
00:39:11,880 --> 00:39:13,740
Why don't you go test his resolve?

1178
00:39:15,930 --> 00:39:18,300
[Cosmic Squad: Epic Killings]

1179
00:39:23,800 --> 00:39:25,210
Hi, I'd like to use the internet.

1180
00:39:25,210 --> 00:39:28,660
[Article 9 Life Esports Hall]

1181
00:39:47,930 --> 00:39:50,090
[No entry for minors]

1182
00:39:53,880 --> 00:39:54,510
Anyone with pink hair

1183
00:39:54,510 --> 00:39:55,110
came in just now?

1184
00:39:55,110 --> 00:39:56,240
Lend me your jacket.

1185
00:39:57,710 --> 00:39:58,710
Who are you?

1186
00:39:58,760 --> 00:39:59,710
Bro, bro,

1187
00:39:59,710 --> 00:40:01,110
help me out.

1188
00:40:01,550 --> 00:40:02,610
Don't make a sound.

1189
00:40:02,960 --> 00:40:03,670
Thanks.

1190
00:40:07,290 --> 00:40:10,210
[The Wizard of Oz;
Set out on the adventure]

1191
00:40:07,480 --> 00:40:08,480
You, check over there.

1192
00:40:08,480 --> 00:40:09,110
Okay.

1193
00:40:23,030 --> 00:40:23,550
Is he there?

1194
00:40:23,550 --> 00:40:24,150
No.

1195
00:40:24,800 --> 00:40:25,920
What a fast runner.

1196
00:40:26,590 --> 00:40:27,720
Boss, he's not here.

1197
00:40:29,630 --> 00:40:30,230
Let's go!

1198
00:40:50,590 --> 00:40:51,110
Thanks.

1199
00:41:08,800 --> 00:41:09,360
Hey.

1200
00:41:10,840 --> 00:41:12,510
Which part of town are you from?

1201
00:41:12,510 --> 00:41:14,510
How come I've never seen you before?

1202
00:41:15,840 --> 00:41:17,190
Unlike you people,

1203
00:41:17,360 --> 00:41:18,290
I'm a decent guy.

1204
00:41:20,190 --> 00:41:21,230
Has anyone ever told you

1205
00:41:21,230 --> 00:41:22,960
that you have a punchable face?

1206
00:41:23,710 --> 00:41:25,320
What a crappy computer.

1207
00:41:25,710 --> 00:41:26,480
Manager!

1208
00:41:31,800 --> 00:41:32,860
See if it works now.

1209
00:41:53,000 --> 00:41:54,510
[Resume] [Name: Liu Zhengliang]

1210
00:41:54,530 --> 00:41:57,550
[Education Background]
[Work Experience]

1211
00:41:54,590 --> 00:41:55,550
Good for you.

1212
00:41:55,880 --> 00:41:57,080
You have a doctorate?

1213
00:41:57,960 --> 00:41:59,400
A medical doctor, huh.

1214
00:42:00,190 --> 00:42:01,650
Is it any of your business?

1215
00:42:04,190 --> 00:42:06,110
No, it's not.

1216
00:42:07,510 --> 00:42:09,070
As a medical doctor,

1217
00:42:10,630 --> 00:42:13,280
you're carrying a coat covered in blood
while looking

1218
00:42:13,280 --> 00:42:14,810
for a job in an esports hall.

1219
00:42:20,110 --> 00:42:21,770
You truly are not faring well.

1220
00:42:22,190 --> 00:42:23,480
What's wrong with you?

1221
00:42:23,880 --> 00:42:25,140
Who's not faring well?

1222
00:42:26,150 --> 00:42:28,360
I'm just under special circumstances

1223
00:42:28,920 --> 00:42:30,920
and temporarily stranded. You know?

1224
00:42:30,920 --> 00:42:32,000
Are you even aware

1225
00:42:32,000 --> 00:42:33,000
how high in demand

1226
00:42:33,000 --> 00:42:33,840
a talent like me is,

1227
00:42:33,840 --> 00:42:34,840
little punk?

1228
00:42:36,440 --> 00:42:37,320
Yeah, right.

1229
00:42:37,960 --> 00:42:39,840
Y-You really are a talent.

1230
00:42:42,920 --> 00:42:44,450
Why am I even talking to you?

1231
00:42:44,800 --> 00:42:45,710
Go as far as you can.

1232
00:42:45,710 --> 00:42:46,230
Bother me again,

1233
00:42:46,230 --> 00:42:47,480
and I'll have that bald man come back.

1234
00:42:47,480 --> 00:42:48,230
Old-timer,

1235
00:42:48,960 --> 00:42:49,760
you see,

1236
00:42:49,840 --> 00:42:51,710
they've gone far away now.

1237
00:42:52,670 --> 00:42:53,760
You think you can scare me?

1238
00:42:53,760 --> 00:42:55,360
Who are you calling an old-timer?

1239
00:42:55,360 --> 00:42:56,110
I'm only 34.

1240
00:42:57,880 --> 00:42:59,440
I just turned 18 this year.

1241
00:42:59,630 --> 00:43:00,840
My mother's 36.

1242
00:43:01,710 --> 00:43:02,970
And you said you're 34.

1243
00:43:03,400 --> 00:43:05,510
H-How else am I supposed to call you?

1244
00:43:06,360 --> 00:43:07,670
I can't call you buddy,

1245
00:43:08,360 --> 00:43:08,840
can I?

1246
00:43:10,760 --> 00:43:12,320
Y-You just do your thing.
